# The frappe_whatsapp this project ships. Sourced by builds.yml (the published
# image) and .github/helper/install.sh (the server-test lane), through
# scripts/fetch-frappe-whatsapp.sh, so CI proves the code the image contains.
#
# Upstream, unmodified: https://github.com/shridarpatil/frappe_whatsapp (MIT).
# No fork. Pinned by commit because no tag will do: the newest tag, v1.0.11,
# predates the multi-account work -- no tag contains the WhatsApp Account doctype
# or WhatsApp Message.whatsapp_account, and per-rep numbers are built on both.
# Upstream's __version__ reads 1.0.12 on master but v1.0.12 was never tagged.
# Move to a tag as soon as one contains this commit.
#
# bench takes a branch or a tag, never a commit, so the commit is parked on a
# local branch exactly as scripts/frappe-pin.env does for frappe.
#
# To move the pin: read upstream's diff of utils/webhook.py and of the WhatsApp
# Message and WhatsApp Account doctypes, since crm/integrations/whatsapp/webhook.py
# depends on how they behave -- in particular on post() logging its
# "Webhook" WhatsApp Notification Log row first, which is the second lock on an
# unsigned request. Change the ref here only, and run crm/tests/test_whatsapp_real.py.
FRAPPE_WHATSAPP_REPO="${FRAPPE_WHATSAPP_REPO:-https://github.com/shridarpatil/frappe_whatsapp}"

# master @ 2026-08-04, __version__ 1.0.12
FRAPPE_WHATSAPP_REF="${FRAPPE_WHATSAPP_REF:-08bc1f6af2e36022d7a5f77641c8ba2ef8c16aaa}"

FRAPPE_WHATSAPP_PIN_BRANCH="${FRAPPE_WHATSAPP_PIN_BRANCH:-pinned}"
